#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:6
msgid "2nd Brain — Persistent Memory System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:8
msgid "What This Is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:9
msgid ""
"`~/brain/` (resolves to `/home/ubuntu/datro/static/llmwiki/` on this "
"server) is the shared intelligence between all agents on this machine. "
"Everything we learn flows through here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:12
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Important:** The brain path may vary by user profile. Always use "
"`~/brain/` or `${BRAIN_ROOT}` rather than hardcoding "
"`/home/ubuntu/datro/static/llmwiki/`. On this machine, the home directory"
" is `/home/ubuntu`, not `/home/unclehowell`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Memory Architecture (3 tiers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:17
msgid "Tier 1: Hermes Memory Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:18
msgid "survives sessions via memory tool (add/replace/remove actions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Two targets: \"memory\" (facts, lessons) and \"user\" (preferences, "
"corrections)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:20
msgid "queried via session_search across all past sessions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:21
msgid "fast, searchable, always injected into context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:23
msgid "Tier 2: Brain Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:24
msgid "~/brain/memory/ — structured memory files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:25
msgid "~/brain/memory/archive/learned/ — dated lesson archives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:26
msgid "synced to GitHub via ~/brain/scripts/sync.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:27
msgid "accessible to ALL agents (hermes, claude, opencode, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:29
msgid "Tier 3: Skills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:30
msgid "~/brain/skills/ — procedural memory (how-to guides)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:31
msgid "loaded via skill_view(name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:32
msgid "created via skill_manage(action=\"create\") when workflows repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:34
msgid "The Closed Loop Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:36
msgid "AT SESSION START:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:37
msgid "Load this skill (2nd-brain)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:38
msgid "Run session_search to check for relevant past sessions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Read ${BRAIN_ROOT}/memory/context/current.md for active priorities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:40
msgid "Load relevant skills matching the task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:42
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"DURING WORK: 5. Save durable facts immediately with "
"memory(action=\"add\") 6. Save user corrections with "
"memory(action=\"add\", target=\"user\") 7. Discover recurring pattern? "
"Create a skill in ${BRAIN_ROOT}/skills/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"AFTER TASK COMPLETION: 8. Write a brief summary to "
"${BRAIN_ROOT}/memory/archive/learned/YYYY-MM-DD/agent-name.md 9. Run: "
"bash ~/brain/scripts/sync.sh 10. Sync must complete before session ends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:52
msgid "Quick Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:54
msgid "Recall past learnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:55
msgid "session_search query=\"keywords OR topics\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:57
msgid "Load a skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:58
msgid "skills_list [category=devops] skill_view name=skill-name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:61
msgid "Save a durable fact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:62
msgid "Write to brain memory files or archive directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:64
msgid "Archive to brain (cross-agent sharing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Write to ${BRAIN_ROOT}/memory/archive/learned/YYYY-MM-DD/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:67
msgid "Close the loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:68
msgid "bash ~/brain/scripts/sync.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:70
msgid "Wiring (do this once)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:72
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Symlink brain skills into Hermes profile skills dir: ln -sf "
"~/brain/skills /home/ubuntu/.hermes/profiles/{profile}/skills/_brain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:75
msgid ""
"CRITICAL: The symlink must go into the PROFILE skills dir "
"(~/.hermes/profiles/*/skills/), NOT into ~/.hermes/skills/. The profile "
"dir is where Hermes actually discovers skills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"Ensure 2nd-brain/skills/brain-sync have SKILL.md files. The 2nd-brain "
"directory will exist but may be EMPTY (no SKILL.md) after a git sync. If "
"SKILL.md is missing, recreate it before loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:82
msgid ""
"Deploy Hermes post-session hook (fires agent:end, session:end): "
"~.hermes/hooks/brain-sync/HOOK.yaml + handler.py This auto-archives "
"session summaries to brain and syncs to GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:86
msgid "Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"The old sync.sh used `git reset --hard origin/main` which WIPES "
"uncommitted local changes. The fixed version uses stash -> pull --rebase "
"-> pop. If you see local changes vanishing after sync, this is the bug. "
"Re-check git status after every sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:92
msgid ""
"Brain files are PUBLIC on GitHub. .env is in .gitignore but verify before"
" committing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"The archive/learned/ folder can go stale — agents skip archiving if dirs "
"dont exist. Always create dirs first with mkdir -p."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/2nd-brain_SKILL.md:96
msgid ""
"Hermes memory tool session-level store and brain files are NOT "
"automatically synced. An agent must explicitly write to BOTH to close the"
" loop fully."
msgstr ""

